	(text "External Power: \nUse only one at a time (USB-C or DC-Jack)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 73.914 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "92de00dd-de1a-44f4-9c06-24658ccaeb91")
	)
	(text "IC Variant\n----------\nTPS259823ONRGE \nhas over voltage lockout threshold = 7.6V w/ circuit breaker\nthis combination provides over voltage protection for > 7.6V (if TLV6700 fails) \n\n\nUnder voltage protection\n----------------------------\nR_VL1 and R_VL2 form a divider from IN to the EN/UVLO pin. \nIt sets the input voltage below which the eFuse keeps its output off\n\nThe EN/UVLO pin has a comparator with a rising threshold of 1.2 V typical (1.18-1.23 V) \nand a falling threshold of 1.1 V typical (1.08-1.13 V). \nThe divider scales the input down so the pin crosses those thresholds at the input voltages \nyou choose:\n\nV_IN(on) = V_UVLO(R) × (R_VL1 + R_VL2) / R_VL2\nV_IN(off) = V_UVLO(F) × (R_VL1 + R_VL2) / R_VL2\n\nThe 0.1 V hysteresis at the pin gets multiplied by the divider ratio, \nwhich gives you useful hysteresis at the input.\n\nChoose R_VL1 = 100k and R_VL2 = 36.5k gives, R_VL1 = R217, R_VL2 = R218\nV_IN(on) = 4.5V\nV_IN(off) = 4.11V. \n\n\nCurrent monitor output\n-----------------------\nR_IMON = V_IMON/(I_OUT * 246uA/A)\nChoose V_IMON = 3.0V,  I_OUT = 6.3A (worst case)\nR_IMON = 3.0/(6.3 * 246e-6) = 1935 Ohm or about 2k, R_IMON = R221\nSo we get 0-3V signal proportional to current\n\nLow pass filter:\nR222 = 10k,   C148 = 100nF, => tau = 1.0ms => f_cut = 160Hz\n\nWetting current\n----------------\nMoved switch to R_VL1, R_VL2 leg.  Added current path via 1k resistor to\nground when device is on to give 5mA wetting current for switch with\nsilver contacts. \n\nPossible Connections to Teensy\n-------------------------------\nPG (Power Good) - with this we can monitor and wait until PG asserted to enable LEDs\nIMON (Current Monitor)- this could be routed to an analog input for current monitoring. \n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.42 345.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(thickness 0.3556)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9483e3df-4499-40a7-952f-5f44083b29e0")
	)
	(text "Power rails for \nbipolar analog inputs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 94.488 185.928 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "9881fa1f-f3b3-4106-9b2f-56b87784cf02")
	)
	(text "\nTrip Current\n------------\nR_ILIM = 1460/(I_ILIM - 0.11),   R_ILIM = R219 on schematic\nSelect trip current to about 5.5A somewhat above the RPI 5A limit. \nChoose I_ILIM = 5.5A => R_ILIM = 1460/(5.5 - 0.11) = 270.8 Ohms. \nClosest E96 value <= is  270 Ohms this gives\nI_ILIM = 5.52A w/ R_ILIM = 270 Ohms\n\n\nInrush and startup\n------------------\nSR (V/ms) = I_INRUSH / C_OUT (uF)\nC_dVdt (pF) = 4600 / SR (V/ms)\n\nChoose C_dVdt = 10nF =>  SR  = 0.46 (V/ms), C_dVdt = C146 on schematicTLV6710\nand assume worst case C_OUT = 2000uF \n\nT_RAMP  = 5V/0.46 = 10.9 ms\nI_INRUSH = 2000uF * 0.46 V/ms = 0.92A\n\n\nCircuit Breaker\n----------------\nfault blanking interval for when load exceeds I_LIM but less the fast-trip (2.1*I_LIM)\n\nT_BLANKING  = C_ITIMER * Delta_V_ITIMER / I_ITIMER\nwhere I_ITIMER = 2.1uA typical (1.4uA min, 2.8uA max) \nDelta_V_ITIMER = 0.98V\nChoose C_ITIMER = 2.2nF =>  T_BLANKING = 1ms, C_ITIMER = C145 on schematic \n(See note 1 below)\n\nNote, fast trip @ 2.1*I_LIM is 400ns\n\n\nNumber of retries and retry delay\n----------------------------------\nnot for fast-trip events\n\nT_RETRY(us) = 128*[ C_RETRY_DLY(pF)  + 4pF]*V_HYS/I_RETRY_DLY\nwhere V_HYS = 0.75V, I_RETRY_DLY = 2.05 (typical values)\nT_RETRY(us) = 46.8*[ C_RETRY_DLY(pF) + 4pF]\nChoose C_RETRY_DLY = 10nF => T_RETRY = 468ms\nC_RETRY_DLY = C143\n\nC_NRETRY = N * [C_RETRY_DLY(pF) + 4pF]/4 \nChoose N = 8 => C_NRETRY = 10004/4 = 20nF or approx 22nF. \nChecking N =  (4 * 22000)/10004 => 8.8 which quantizes to 16 tries (see spec sheet)  \nC_NRETRY = C144\n\n\nOver voltage protection\n-------------------------\nTLV6710 (window comparator) provides first line of over voltage protection  \nSelect R_OV1 = 150k and R_OV2 = 12k and (internal) 0.4V Threshold give\nV_TRIP = 0.4 V × (1 + R_OV1 / R_OV2) = 0.4 × (1 + 150k / 12k) = 5.40 V\nR_OV1 = R223 , R_OV2 =4 R225\n\n\nNote 1:  There is typo in spec sheet for setting C_ITIMER \nSee link below Section 8.2.2.7 should show the equation and example in one place.\nhttps://www.ti.com/document-viewer/lit/html/SLVSFR1A\n\n\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 47.498 367.03 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(thickness 0.3556)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a84f7246-a778-4047-b22b-cc95fad37845")
	)
